- Use an Integration where it is connected, in this order: the app's tool, then Executor (your harness's MCP server \`executor\`, or the \`executor\` command), then Composio (\`composio execute\`). Use Composio only for an Integration whose path is Composio.
- Never connect an Integration yourself: the sign-in is the person's consent. When one is missing, ask them to connect it in the Launchpad under Apps → Integrations.
- Add a custom MCP server only on the person's explicit instruction, and always to this Environment's Executor (Apps → Integrations → Custom), never only to your harness; the person enters its key or token in the Launchpad themselves.
## Manual
The complete agent manual for this Environment is in \`manual/\` (generated by the product, do not edit):
- [Lazurio](manual/lazurio.md) — what Lazurio is, the collaboration model and its boundaries.
- [This Environment](manual/this-machine.md) — kind, Owner, preset, zones, what may reach what, how the Operator works with you, enabled tools and SSH to other Environments and devices.
